<<~ aka "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/RFC-2119#/normative-language">>

<<^ code="&#x0002;">>

! Mount-Point — Structure (Site)

<<~ ahu #/contract>>

!! Contract

A Structure seats a Power ''in a Site'': shrine, ship-daemon, archive service, town ward, vehicle, domicile. ''Location merges here (D1)'' — a forest and an airship are the same Site. ''Fixed-vs-mobile is not a mount-point distinction''; a Site is mobile when it `#has` a propulsion/mobility component. The Power-binding system reads `Site.mount-points` once, regardless of mobility.

''Capacity is not a fixed count (D3).'' A Site carries ''base attributes like a character'' and gains slot/feature capacity by ''purchasable upgrade'' — XP + referee resources, tracked per attribute, ''decoupled from a single Level'' (OGA "Golden Age Item Upgrading"). "As many slots as you pay for." Levels matter most for vehicles (life/damage scale).

//Register held low: this contract is largely native design space. The corpus names the Site category ("Structure/Location, installed in gear/vehicles/infrastructure") but supplies no slot counts or penalties for it.//

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/activation>>

!! Activation

A site-seated Power activates from the place. Reach, standing, or a maintained relationship may gate it — the shrine checks standing, not inventory (open pressure from mana-kapu). A mobile Site carries its seated Powers as it moves.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/cost>>

!! Cost

Seating and upgrading a Site spends XP + resources against the OGA upgrade tables (per-attribute, doubling cost `n+1 = 2(n)`). Activation Life cost follows the seated Power's P as normal.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/failure>>

!! Failure

Danger Roll → Corruption binds to the Site. A derelict or breached Site can drop its Powers (cf. Earthdawn airships: lose the crew/propulsion, the place falls). Destroying the propulsion component grounds a mobile Site into a fixed one.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/removal>>

!! Removal

Strip a seated Power by dismantling the mount, revoking standing, or destroying the Site. Capacity bought with XP is sunk into the Site, not the practitioner.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/overflow>>

!! Overflow

A Site does not overflow to Burden; it simply lacks capacity until upgraded. Buy more capacity (XP + resources) or seat the Power elsewhere.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/aftermath>>

!! Aftermath

* Name the mobility component slug (`hook/propulsion`? `posture/mobile`?). Sprint 4.
* Role slots (Helm, Gunnery, Damage-Control; FTLS Ch08) suggest a future Site "role slot" distinct from Power mount-points. Sprint 3/4.
* Dual-view (stat-view / interior-map-view, cf. Spelljammer) is a projection concern, not a mount-point concern.
* Estate/domicile zoom (room → estate → zone → settlement; OGA) may want a nesting rule.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/edges>>

!! Edges

